","FEEDBACK_TO_CODEX.md":"1495be660c91715add1446855f7947c6c56c08e12a03683eb2567d1fa58743ab","QUESTION_ANSWER.md":"80b1f7d201df671bb7b85eca8565ea87a5ea41ff5307d7d562799150bd7fda14","REVIEW.md":"ab1ae8aa43376e7f589b542f4d7feff455d7382e84465669dc51ad9e20269d7d","patches/source.patch":"8a8bceda8a66d8596ebd05f9cf07b9f83dc8996180c1718a4490e807947b2e67","solve-blind/FINISHED_NOTES.md":"5a575633a199b6910e45362668b44ad582b879dfd98f7b8703f528a3941d8be6","solve-blind/README.md":"da1025aece84ba55cccf208f41b4b0b3fe1ffe9712b71f4b74c4465d45791173","solve-blind/SOLVE_NOTES.md":"5a575633a199b6910e45362668b44ad582b879dfd98f7b8703f528a3941d8be6","solve-blind/attempts/0001/SOLVE_NOTES.md":"f40ab7e60f50739d78f9bb8cbf36cee135a589a181b5d33c444243ed00297c54","solve-blind/attempts/0001/execution.json":"8d3c3be70385ec6c853d7fc93eff9f98a25a0533d6111271c85229cdbbf8f64f","solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json":"e240ccb57130c33fabd30897d8fd3204ade92b1efae51e813b336681155805cd","solve-blind/attempts/0001/solution.py":"9654018351b55e6241592ad853f7974f272fcd0847c62d4353a2eb23bf0df53d","solve-blind/challenge.json":"c82c4784c20c6217dde048b3b625e01953ca0702c712905b2cece1e36afdc92c","solve-blind/solution.py":"9654018351b55e6241592ad853f7974f272fcd0847c62d4353a2eb23bf0df53d","solve-blind/source/generator.py":"6ee28e89af05de084974a8f474826d3d7e1e8ab76db8f0909c4396b79cb07313","solve-blind/summary.json":"3039c100823befb1dff79ef0d37db96eaa7f1589689d85f525a61c6a4e4eb3e8","solve/FINISHED_NOTES.md":"5bdd07aabc61302e4760b541ae1b258e51d2cb2ceba10241e7a075950364e086","solve/README.md":"502db75e894d9c5872ae9fb401bab8a5805d5875701d6ce1cd556ab3775c62c3","solve/SOLVE_NOTES.md":"5bdd07aabc61302e4760b541ae1b258e51d2cb2ceba10241e7a075950364e086","solve/attempts/0001/SOLVE_NOTES.md":"13df1ebb51d86a6ba0b461413d27c059337d71e4a18c3d3412e68a3f03bda4e3","solve/attempts/0001/execution.json":"8d3c3be70385ec6c853d7fc93eff9f98a25a0533d6111271c85229cdbbf8f64f","solve/attempts/0001/report.json":"d5bad87cb4b2f264c6fb560c0e0b10a512a970a8244a27eeae48cfa020da0df0","solve/attempts/0001/solution.py":"4d7dbcea7107d6926509f80d2c77510c4b6a1d0e66db03e88239260f00be1b63","solve/challenge.json":"bfb747fe40e3fb2e77515fa5fd0001a0590ee5d188e72e853ddd6e40be5ed78b","solve/solution.py":"4d7dbcea7107d6926509f80d2c77510c4b6a1d0e66db03e88239260f00be1b63","solve/source/generator.py":"450d238a82ab2de4b6c808f5f70f966a1667cbdcbf952cf322a826d5dcc51e1d","solve/summary.json":"ee55f7179a5b5f2a0f8010ff8031ba0319d3ee221a70a356188b0483c5c44c1e"},"feedback_items":[{"id":"F1","text":"Distinguish finite structural-support warnings from demonstrated defects — top shared-tool suggestion\n\n**Needs a shared-tool decision.** `shared/runtime/review_diagnostics.py:compare_structure` labels disjoint exact finite sets of component counts an `advisory_mismatch`; `shared/tools/generator_defect_lint.py` promotes it to a warning that blocks strict after acceptance. On final generator `450d238a82ab2de4b6c808f5f70f966a1667cbdcbf952cf322a826d5dcc51e1d`, canonical train counts are {4,12,32} and the 60-call cohort has no exact match, despite broad count ranges and deliberate canonical/diagnostic strata. Only 40 input grids are distinct. This is the sole remaining failed gate; we have not treated it as a pass.\n\nEvidence: `checks/after-final/checks/832404dc8a5c_after_defect_lint.log`, `checks/structural-warning.json`, and the runnable task-local `workspace/probe_structure.py`. The latter reports actual seed/index, dimensions, profile, input hash, count by color, and exact intersections, without changing the gate or claiming interval overlap proves equivalence.\n\nProposed shared change: show canonical-versus-generated distributions conditioned on comparable dimensions/profile or an explicit task structural contract, include unique-input counts, and keep unconditioned finite-set disjointness advisory unless the task declares it invariant. Do not silently weaken existing required checks: update the policy and regression fixtures deliberately. A control with overlapping populations but disjoint finite draws, and a control with a truly forbidden structural feature, should establish the intended distinction. The maintainer must decide this policy; no shared patch is applied here."},{"id":"F2","text":"Exercise answer-equivalent controls and tied witness cases in semantic-contract tests\n\n**Findings-only audit; no shared or peer-source edit.** Audit 9971f3a5882c shows a hook rejecting a lesson because a rival fits the demonstrations even though it also gives the exact query answer. Another accepted input has two same-side markers tied along the relevant distance axis: a coarse multiple-marker predicate fires but nearest/farthest policies agree. The shared semantic-gate documentation already states the correct answer-aware interpretation, so the missing safeguard is targeted contract coverage, not a new definition.\n\nEvidence: `checks/audit/9971f3a5882c/assessment.json`, `probe.json`, and `racket.json` retain the exact inputs and five actual reference outputs. Suggested shared testing controls: require a surviving-rival/different-query negative and a surviving-rival/same-query positive; test each witness's claimed implication on accepted tie and degeneracy mutations as well as ordinary sampler draws. Keep branch coverage separate from actual rival refutation. The main repair already uses query-aware rival checks and explicit executable witnesses."},{"id":"F3","text":"Cross-check advertised control support against every difficulty, including None\n\n**Findings-only audit plus task-local fixes already included for the main generator.** Audit bb1b1e111e1a reproduces an unused `mask_density` control: all three seed-matched pairs at 0.1 versus 0.9 produce identical complete inputs. It also shows the advertised dimension endpoints rejected under `difficulty=None`, while a middle control succeeds. These can mislead downstream agents into assuming requested diversity was generated.\n\nEvidence: `checks/audit/bb1b1e111e1a/probe.json`, `summary.json`, and the exact reference outputs in `racket.json`. Suggested control-suite coverage: enumerate each declared endpoint against None/easy/medium/hard, report effective override provenance, and test distribution controls across paired seeds with a distinct 'unused or statistically indistinguishable' verdict. Preserve explicitly incompatible combinations. Do not infer that all distribution controls must change every single seed. The main task now rejects unknown controls and type coercions, honors exact dimensions across all bands, and declares texture/count incompatibilities.\n\n## Delivered reusable tooling\n\nThe allowed task patch includes the runnable endpoint-threshold prototype, `workspace/probe_curriculum.py`, and `workspace/probe_structure.py`. The curriculum probe dynamically inspects all declared rival namespaces, executes selected Racket labels, checks source stability, records exact grids and first differing cells, and keeps input-only size coverage separate from labeled cases. Its four focused tests include declaration discovery and refusing to overwrite evidence. These tools make the observations above concrete without modifying the shared review infrastructure."},{"id":"F4","text":"Make supported authoring commands compatible with the stock packager\n\nThe first package attempt failed on `repo/REVIEW/.lock`. The supported selected-only authority sync also left a new recovery receipt and original selected JSON under `repo/var/review/authority-sync/`; the stock packager rejects any such untracked file outside the assigned task. These are legitimate command byproducts, not unrelated source edits.\n\nEvidence: `checks/package-candidate.log` and `checks/packaging-generated-files.json`. I moved only those three completed-run files into `checks/packaging-generated-recovery/`, preserving their bytes and hashes, then reran the unchanged packager. After the replay/test workflow, the same generated files were found again across multiple attempts; one attempted cleanup also observed `repo/REVIEW/.rsync-tmp/.lock` and aborted on that unknown path. Their exact recreation cause was not isolated. The failed attempts remain under `checks/package-final-*.log`. A duplicate full extraction exhausted the overlay inode limit and was removed. I then used an isolated hardlink snapshot: it verifies the original ZIP and manifest, hashes all 99,605 declared workspace files against the original or exact tested-change hashes, materializes the complete declared source inventory, and copies reports/evidence. The unchanged stock packager runs there. This conserves inodes and avoids live untracked byproducts. The reusable helper and hash-checked preparation receipt are under `checks/isolated-packaging/`; it does not modify the packager, ignore unknown source files, or change any gate. The recovery original and apply receipt remain in the return. Suggested shared change: route authoring recovery records outside the source inventory from creation, and treat a completed advisory lock as runtime state with an explicit policy. Do not broadly ignore unknown repository paths or weaken immutable-source checks."}],"packet_id":"6d4bcfef35cbdd009443c1d190c586508065c404d2cab90ac7cbf9431f3eb0c1","reviewer_blind_solve":{"attempt_count":1,"attempt_intents":{"solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json":"solve"},"attempt_reports":["solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json"],"earlier_rule_exposure":"no","feedback_policy":"visible_only","generator_hash":"6ee28e89af05de084974a8f474826d3d7e1e8ab76db8f0909c4396b79cb07313","instance_hash":"6f8ef613c4f887d03efa405a7144834b3c492fb38664432859271605f328e543","reference_consulted_during_solve":false,"solve_kind":"blind_before_repair","source_kind":"reviewer_authored","status":"finished","task_id":"a16e387b682a"},"reviewer_solve":{"attempt_count":1,"attempt_intents":{"solve/attempts/0001/report.json":"solve"},"attempt_reports":["solve/attempts/0001/report.json"],"earlier_rule_exposure":"yes","feedback_p